      "text": "Cocenters and representations of affine Hecke algebra — In this paper, we study the relation between the cocenter and the representation theory of aﬃne Hecke algebras.\n\n**Cocenters and representations of affine Hecke algebra**\n\n*DAN CIUBOTARU AND XUHUAHE*\n\n31 pp, 51 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** In this paper, we study the relation between the cocenter and the representation theory of aﬃne Hecke algebras. The appro ach is based on the interaction between the rigid cocenter, an important subspace of the cocenter, and the dual object in representation theory, the rigid quotient of the Grothendieck group of ﬁnite dimensional representatio ns.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1.; 1.2.; 1.3.; 1.4.; 1.5.; 2 Preliminaries; 2.1.; 2.2.; 2.3.; 2.4.; 3.1.; 3.2.; 3.3.; 3.4.; 4 Induction and restriction; 4.1.\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 1.1: (1) The set{TO :O∈ cl(~W )0} is a basis of ¯Hrigid for an aﬃne\n- Theorem 1.1: in particular explains where the name “rigid” for ¯Hrigid comes from:\n- Theorem 1.2: The set {TO :O ∈cl(~W )} is a basis of ¯H for an aﬃne Hecke\n- Theorem 1.3: (1) (Density Theorem) Suppose that the parameters of the aﬃne\n- Theorem 3.3: (1) If X is an irreducible H-module\n- Theorem 5.1: LetO be a conjugacy class of ~W ′ andOmin be the set of minimal",
